  "body": "Deadline sale: Closes on Wednesday 28 October 2026 at 3:00PM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nWho says an entry-level home can’t have a little extra?\r\n\r\nZoned for Rangitoto College, this end-terrace at 74E Langana Ave is one of those homes that makes you rethink what “entry-level” really means.\r\n\r\nThe standout extra? A separate ground-level flexi room with its own ensuite, alongside the double internal-access garage. Perfect for teenagers wanting their own space, extended family needing a little independence, a work-from-home setup, or simply a bit more room for everyone.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, multiple living areas and good-sized bedrooms give a growing family room to spread out and find their own corners, while still coming together at the end of the day. The kids can take over one living area, while Mum and Dad enjoy a little peace and quiet in another. There’s flexibility here to suit different stages of family life.\r\n\r\nAnd being an end terrace adds that little bit of extra breathing room too.\r\n\r\nThe double garage is another practical bonus. No squeezing everything into a single garage and hoping the bikes, scooters and weekend gear somehow disappear! There’s room for parking, storage and all the bits that come with family life.\r\n\r\nAdd the Rangitoto College zone, a seriously generous floor plan, the extra downstairs space and the remaining Master Build Guarantee, and you’ve got a pretty compelling package for families wanting to get into a sought-after school zone without compromising on space.\r\n\r\nA little more than you’d expect\r\n- Rangitoto College zone\r\n- Seriously generous floor plan\r\n- Ground-level flexi room with its own ensuite\r\n- End-terrace position\r\n- Double internal-access garage\r\n- Remaining Master Build Guarantee\r\n- Handy Browns Bay location, close to local shops, beaches, schools and everyday essentials\r\n\r\nIt’s not just about getting into a sought-after school zone. It’s about having more space, more flexibility and more options for the future.\r\n\r\nFor a growing family, that extra room downstairs could make all the difference.\r\n\r\nCome and see it for yourself. You might be surprised just how much house — and potential — you get here!",
